WEBVTT

1
01:06:47.906 --> 01:06:50.906
A bottle is already open and I just drank a whole bottle myself.

2
01:06:51.906 --> 01:06:53.906
I am not going to drink from someone else's bottle.

3
01:06:55.906 --> 01:06:56.906
Hallelujah.

4
01:06:57.906 --> 01:06:58.906
Praise God.

5
01:06:59.906 --> 01:07:01.906
Is everyone ready for God's Word?

6
01:07:02.906 --> 01:07:04.906
Please show your Bible.

7
01:07:06.906 --> 01:07:08.906
Okay, hold it up for a moment, okay?

8
01:07:08.906 --> 01:07:09.906
Hold it up for a moment, okay?

9
01:07:10.906 --> 01:07:11.906
Here is another question.

10
01:07:11.906 --> 01:07:16.906
Hold it up if you have read it in the Bible this week.

11
01:07:18.906 --> 01:07:22.906
Raise your hand if you don't have your Bible with you, but you have read it in the Bible.

12
01:07:22.906 --> 01:07:23.906
Raise your hand.

13
01:07:23.906 --> 01:07:24.906
Good job.

14
01:07:25.906 --> 01:07:27.906
Raise your hand if you haven't read the Bible.

15
01:07:27.906 --> 01:07:28.906
No, well, I was shocked.

16
01:07:29.906 --> 01:07:30.906
I was shocked.

17
01:07:35.906 --> 01:07:36.906
Wonderful.

18
01:07:36.906 --> 01:07:41.906
God's Word is the foundation of your life.

19
01:07:42.906 --> 01:07:44.906
For God's Word is Jesus Himself.

20
01:07:44.906 --> 01:07:46.906
And He is the rock on which we build. Amen.

21
01:07:48.906 --> 01:07:57.906
Today, dear Open Church, I will talk to you about the past weekend.

22
01:07:57.906 --> 01:08:03.906
And a number of things I discussed with the leaders of Open Church.

23
01:08:03.906 --> 01:08:10.906
Last weekend, we went on retreat with the group of leaders.

24
01:08:11.906 --> 01:08:14.906
And we do that once a year.

25
01:08:14.906 --> 01:08:18.906
For four, four or five, four years now.

26
01:08:19.906 --> 01:08:24.906
We take the leaders on a leadership weekend somewhere in the Kempen.

27
01:08:25.906 --> 01:08:27.906
Because this church is called Open Church.

28
01:08:28.906 --> 01:08:35.906
And Open Church does not mean very positively, oh, we are open and everything and everyone and it's all very nice.

29
01:08:36.906 --> 01:08:39.906
Yes, you are welcome, but that is not why we named Open Church Open Church.

30
01:08:40.906 --> 01:08:48.906
In 1983, this church was founded and the Holy Spirit gave the name Rehoboth to this church.

31
01:08:49.906 --> 01:08:56.906
My parents did not yet know at that time that Rehoboth and Kempen are actually the same name.

32
01:08:57.906 --> 01:09:01.906
Because Kempen comes from the Latin word Campina.

33
01:09:01.906 --> 01:09:03.906
You probably know the milk brand Campina, I think.

34
01:09:04.906 --> 01:09:06.906
Well, Campina is a Latin word.

35
01:09:06.906 --> 01:09:14.906
And the Roman generals came with horses and wagons from Leuven and from the Ardennes into this area.

36
01:09:15.906 --> 01:09:24.906
And instead of forests and hills and mountains, they found themselves on the plains, the heathland.

37
01:09:25.906 --> 01:09:28.906
If you take a walk behind this area, you will come to the Plateauheide.

38
01:09:28.906 --> 01:09:31.906
Well, that is actually what the whole Kempen looks like.

39
01:09:32.906 --> 01:09:38.906
Large pieces of land, heathland with a bit less forest, flat areas.

40
01:09:39.906 --> 01:09:43.906
And the Roman generals said, hey, we will call this piece Campina.

41
01:09:43.906 --> 01:09:47.906
For Campina, Kempen, means open area.

42
01:09:48.906 --> 01:09:49.906
An open plain.

43
01:09:50.906 --> 01:10:06.906
And when I was doing my studies at Hillsong, Australia, I had to write an essay about the area I came from and its socio-historical and spiritual background, the context of it.

44
01:10:06.906 --> 01:10:12.906
And in my research, I found out, and here comes the cool part, so Campina means open area.

45
01:10:13.906 --> 01:10:35.906
And Rehoboth was a well that was dug, and it was spoken of, Rehoboth is an open area where worship is, where there will be unity, where there will be no quarrels, and a place where we can come together to worship.

46
01:10:35.906 --> 01:10:39.906
That is the Old Testament word Rehoboth.

47
01:10:39.906 --> 01:10:49.906
And so the cool thing is that the Holy Spirit has given a clear mandate for this church to establish itself here in our generation.

48
01:10:49.906 --> 01:11:01.906
And the Holy Spirit has said, your outreach area, your area of responsibility is Rehoboth, is the Kempen, is Campina the open area where we are placed.

49
01:11:02.906 --> 01:11:16.906
And when Vanessa and I took over the church, I did not want to let go of the Old Testament word Rehoboth, because that was clearly something the Holy Spirit had given.

50
01:11:16.906 --> 01:11:27.906
Only in the common language of today, in the modern times we live in, where fewer and fewer people in our society are Christians, but that will change in the name of Jesus.

51
01:11:28.906 --> 01:11:32.906
There are already people in the village saying, where are you going? Yes, we are going to Rehoboth.

52
01:11:32.906 --> 01:11:36.906
Oh, Rehoboth, what is that? People do not understand that.

53
01:11:36.906 --> 01:11:47.906
And so I have named this church with the mandate of the Holy Spirit and the meaning of the name Rehoboth, and that means open church.

54
01:11:47.906 --> 01:11:52.906
That we will be an open area of worship, where there will be no quarrels.

55
01:11:52.906 --> 01:11:56.906
This is a safe church in the mighty name of Jesus. Amen.

56
01:11:58.906 --> 01:12:00.906
And that is why this church is called open church.

57
01:12:00.906 --> 01:12:07.906
And yes, you are welcome to come. And yes, you are welcome as you are and who you were.

58
01:12:07.906 --> 01:12:12.906
But you are welcome here to come to be washed by the blood of Jesus.

59
01:12:12.906 --> 01:12:17.906
And to think differently and live differently through the Word of God.

60
01:12:17.906 --> 01:12:20.906
That you are washed by the Word of God. Amen.

61
01:12:21.906 --> 01:12:27.906
Last weekend we went to the Leaders Weekend with the leaders.

62
01:12:27.906 --> 01:12:31.906
And then we take the leaders to one of the villages in the Kempen.

63
01:12:31.906 --> 01:12:37.906
The Kempen is quite large. The Kempen stretches from Bree all the way to Antwerp.

64
01:12:37.906 --> 01:12:43.906
So that is really, during peak times, completely, but anyway, that is really about an hour and fifteen minutes drive.

65
01:12:43.906 --> 01:12:46.906
If you have to drive all the way from Bree to Antwerp, then you are busy for a while.

66
01:12:46.906 --> 01:12:49.906
And that is about from Eindhoven to Hasselt.

67
01:12:49.906 --> 01:12:52.906
So that is the Kempen. That is quite a large area.

68
01:12:52.906 --> 01:12:56.906
And then we take the leaders to one of the villages.

69
01:12:56.906 --> 01:13:00.906
And then we will gather there to pray together.

70
01:13:00.906 --> 01:13:04.906
To talk together about the work we are allowed to do in Open Church.

71
01:13:04.906 --> 01:13:08.906
The calling we have as leaders in Open Church.

72
01:13:08.906 --> 01:13:10.906
And then we encourage each other.

73
01:13:10.906 --> 01:13:13.906
We have a good time. Of course, there is good food.

74
01:13:13.906 --> 01:13:16.906
Because we all love that. Amen.

75
01:13:16.906 --> 01:13:18.906
But then we really have a nice time.

76
01:13:18.906 --> 01:13:24.906
In the past few years, we are now in our tenth year that Vanessa and I are allowed to do this.

77
01:13:24.906 --> 01:13:29.906
And I have sometimes called leaders' evenings together.

78
01:13:29.906 --> 01:13:32.906
It is important that you come together as a leader.

79
01:13:32.906 --> 01:13:35.906
And then I would do, for example, I called it a core night back then.

80
01:13:35.906 --> 01:13:39.906
The core is the trunk, so it is the foundation.

81
01:13:39.906 --> 01:13:44.906
And then I organized those kinds of leaders' evenings here in the church.

82
01:13:44.906 --> 01:13:47.906
But then you have the busyness of life.

83
01:13:47.906 --> 01:13:50.906
People work hard. People are already serving here.

84
01:13:50.906 --> 01:13:52.906
Every week. Week in, week out.

85
01:13:52.906 --> 01:13:55.906
Here in this place. Every time working hard.

86
01:13:55.906 --> 01:13:57.906
Because the people work hard for you.

87
01:13:57.906 --> 01:13:59.906
The leaders are really great.

88
01:13:59.906 --> 01:14:03.906
And then I noticed every time, I organized a leaders' evening.

89
01:14:03.906 --> 01:14:07.906
And then we would bring some food and so on. Then we made it cozy.

90
01:14:07.906 --> 01:14:11.906
But then I noticed in that fatigue, you get like, yes.

91
01:14:11.906 --> 01:14:15.906
Then they are half yawning and I am sitting there with sweat on my forehead yelling.

92
01:14:15.906 --> 01:14:17.906
And then I thought, yes, this is just not it.

93
01:14:17.906 --> 01:14:19.906
And why is it just not it?

94
01:14:19.906 --> 01:14:23.906
Because you want something, you want to create a piece of intimacy.

95
01:14:23.906 --> 01:14:25.906
You want to take them aside.

96
01:14:25.906 --> 01:14:29.906
Jesus had intimacy with his disciples for three years.

97
01:14:29.906 --> 01:14:33.906
It wasn't that the disciples saw Jesus every Sunday.

98
01:14:33.906 --> 01:14:37.906
No, they saw Jesus day in and day out.

99
01:14:37.906 --> 01:14:39.906
Walking together with each other.

100
01:14:39.906 --> 01:14:42.906
And that is how the congregation of Christ should be with each other.

101
01:14:42.906 --> 01:14:44.906
And that is such a nice time.

102
01:14:44.906 --> 01:14:47.906
Leaders, is it true? It has been a nice weekend, hasn't it?

103
01:14:47.906 --> 01:14:49.906
Yes, really good.

104
01:14:49.906 --> 01:14:53.906
And every time we then provide a piece of teaching from SNHK.

105
01:14:53.906 --> 01:14:55.906
And we pray together.

106
01:14:55.906 --> 01:14:58.906
And there is really unity. And I find that so cool.

107
01:14:58.906 --> 01:15:05.906
And the theme of this weekend, I had really given it a title.

108
01:15:05.906 --> 01:15:07.906
And I want to share that with you.

109
01:15:07.906 --> 01:15:10.906
Because it is of course good that if I discuss something with the leaders,

110
01:15:10.906 --> 01:15:15.906
that I also communicate that to the congregation in the same measure.

111
01:15:15.906 --> 01:15:20.906
So that you know that we are really doing our best for the congregation.

112
01:15:20.906 --> 01:15:22.906
We are really doing our best.

113
01:15:22.906 --> 01:15:24.906
A lot of hours go into it.

114
01:15:24.906 --> 01:15:26.906
A lot of prayers go into it.

115
01:15:26.906 --> 01:15:28.906
A lot of energy goes into it.

116
01:15:28.906 --> 01:15:30.906
There is dedication in it.

117
01:15:30.906 --> 01:15:31.906
And that is important.

118
01:15:31.906 --> 01:15:34.906
Because it is not a feel-good movement.

119
01:15:34.906 --> 01:15:36.906
It is the church of Jesus Christ.

120
01:15:36.906 --> 01:15:41.906
And in the church of Jesus Christ, people can come as they were.

121
01:15:41.906 --> 01:15:43.906
to be benefited in God's Word.

122
01:15:43.906 --> 01:15:46.906
And to ultimately be restored in atonement with the Father.

123
01:15:46.906 --> 01:15:49.906
That is amazing work that we get to do.

124
01:15:49.906 --> 01:15:50.906
That is a calling.

125
01:15:50.906 --> 01:15:54.906
And the theme of this weekend I had proclaimed.

126
01:15:54.906 --> 01:15:57.906
And its title was

127
01:15:57.906 --> 01:16:00.906
Pay attention, the church is growing.

128
01:16:00.906 --> 01:16:04.906
Pay attention, the church is growing.

129
01:16:05.906 --> 01:16:08.906
And I have indeed said to the leaders.

130
01:16:08.906 --> 01:16:12.906
I am not saying, great, the church is growing.

131
01:16:12.906 --> 01:16:15.906
It is great.

132
01:16:15.906 --> 01:16:18.906
I am not saying, hallelujah, how wonderful we are.

133
01:16:18.906 --> 01:16:20.906
The church is growing.

134
01:16:20.906 --> 01:16:23.906
I did not say, wow, how well we are doing.

135
01:16:23.906 --> 01:16:25.906
The church is growing.

136
01:16:25.906 --> 01:16:29.906
I did not say, gee, how nice, success.

137
01:16:29.906 --> 01:16:30.906
The church is growing.

138
01:16:30.906 --> 01:16:32.906
And that is all true.

139
01:16:32.906 --> 01:16:37.906
But I said to the leaders, pay attention, the church is growing.

140
01:16:37.906 --> 01:16:41.906
Because a growing church, before you know it,

141
01:16:41.906 --> 01:16:44.906
do you think together, while you sit in a hall,

142
01:16:44.906 --> 01:16:46.906
and people are already sitting at the back on a bench,

143
01:16:46.906 --> 01:16:49.906
and there are people already in the overflowing lounge area.

144
01:16:49.906 --> 01:16:51.906
We are working on a construction project.

145
01:16:51.906 --> 01:16:53.906
And before you know it, you all end up

146
01:16:53.906 --> 01:16:56.906
in a kind of flow of thinking

147
01:16:56.906 --> 01:16:59.906
that we are having such a good time, and it is so wonderful.

148
01:16:59.906 --> 01:17:03.906
And before you know it, that becomes the focus.

149
01:17:03.906 --> 01:17:05.906
That if we just have more people,

150
01:17:05.906 --> 01:17:07.906
and if we have a good time together,

151
01:17:07.906 --> 01:17:10.906
and if the worship is good, and then we do the worship well,

152
01:17:10.906 --> 01:17:12.906
and if we then have a good set,

153
01:17:12.906 --> 01:17:14.906
and the people are singing nicely together,

154
01:17:14.906 --> 01:17:17.906
yes, that was a nice time.

155
01:17:17.906 --> 01:17:20.906
But actually, that should not be the focus.

156
01:17:20.906 --> 01:17:25.906
The focus is not the experience.

157
01:17:25.906 --> 01:17:29.906
The focus is not the experience on Sunday morning.

158
01:17:29.906 --> 01:17:31.906
That is not the focus.

159
01:17:31.906 --> 01:17:34.906
As the pastor of this church, I may not measure the church,

160
01:17:34.906 --> 01:17:37.906


161
01:17:37.906 --> 01:17:39.906
if I were to say a success meter,

162
01:17:39.906 --> 01:17:43.906
I must not measure the church by how great a service was.

163
01:17:43.906 --> 01:17:48.906
I must not measure the church by how many people we have.

164
01:17:48.906 --> 01:17:50.906
I must not measure the church by that.

165
01:17:50.906 --> 01:17:53.906
I also do not want to measure the church by finances,

166
01:17:53.906 --> 01:17:55.906
or by the number of seats.

167
01:17:55.906 --> 01:17:57.906
I do not want to measure the church by that.

168
01:17:57.906 --> 01:18:02.906
I want to know if the church of Jesus Christ is healthy,

169
01:18:02.906 --> 01:18:06.906
by looking at whether people are changing in the name of Jesus,

170
01:18:06.906 --> 01:18:10.906
washed by the Word.

171
01:18:10.906 --> 01:18:16.906
And that is why I said to the leaders, pay attention, the church is growing.

172
01:18:16.906 --> 01:18:20.906
For a growing church sounds nice,

173
01:18:20.906 --> 01:18:24.906
but there are all kinds of people, just like you and me, who are joining.

174
01:18:24.906 --> 01:18:27.906
And on one hand, that is nice,

175
01:18:27.906 --> 01:18:29.906
but all kinds of people are joining.

176
01:18:29.906 --> 01:18:33.906
And those people come from the world,

177
01:18:33.906 --> 01:18:35.906
they walk into the church,

178
01:18:35.906 --> 01:18:38.906
and other people come from other churches,

179
01:18:38.906 --> 01:18:40.906
in one way or another.

180
01:18:40.906 --> 01:18:41.906
That can be disappointing,

181
01:18:41.906 --> 01:18:45.906
that can be dysfunction from other churches.

182
01:18:45.906 --> 01:18:47.906
It can be for all sorts of reasons,

183
01:18:47.906 --> 01:18:49.906
legitimate reasons or not so legitimate reasons,

184
01:18:49.906 --> 01:18:53.906
but people also come from other churches to Open Church.

185
01:18:53.906 --> 01:18:56.906
And people have a backpack, do you understand what I mean?

186
01:18:56.906 --> 01:19:01.906
People come with their baggage, with their context, is a good word.

187
01:19:01.906 --> 01:19:05.906
People come with who they are, they come to Open Church.

188
01:19:05.906 --> 01:19:09.906
And on one hand, that is amazing.

189
01:19:09.906 --> 01:19:14.906
I said this weekend, it just makes me happy,

190
01:19:14.906 --> 01:19:16.906
when I look around in the church.

191
01:19:16.906 --> 01:19:19.906
And I see men turning into godly men.

192
01:19:19.906 --> 01:19:22.906
Oh, that makes me so, I just get a kick out of it.

193
01:19:22.906 --> 01:19:26.906
To see how men are actually broken,

194
01:19:26.906 --> 01:19:29.906
and through paganism just a knife.

195
01:19:29.906 --> 01:19:34.906
While you see in a man that, wow, there is so much potential in him.

196
01:19:34.906 --> 01:19:36.906
If only men would become godly men,

197
01:19:36.906 --> 01:19:37.906
priests of their family.

198
01:19:37.906 --> 01:19:39.906
Yes, I'm speaking for the men for a moment.

199
01:19:39.906 --> 01:19:43.906
Then boy, really, something truly wonderful arises.

200
01:19:43.906 --> 01:19:45.906
Then a force arises.

201
01:19:46.906 --> 01:19:49.906
Whereby the generations can grow up.

202
01:19:49.906 --> 01:19:51.906
And can look at dad.

203
01:19:51.906 --> 01:19:56.906
And it is so wonderful when godly men can simply receive respect

204
01:19:56.906 --> 01:19:58.906
from their wives and from their children.

205
01:19:58.906 --> 01:20:02.906
And that those children want to be like their dad, that is wonderful.

206
01:20:02.906 --> 01:20:06.906
Instead of those children thinking, I am ashamed of my father.

207
01:20:06.906 --> 01:20:08.906
And how often do you see that in the world?

208
01:20:08.906 --> 01:20:12.906
That dads misbehave, or do not stay with their children.

209
01:20:12.906 --> 01:20:14.906
But not in Open Church.

210
01:20:14.906 --> 01:20:17.906
For in Open Church we want to work hard on that.

211
01:20:17.906 --> 01:20:19.906
That men and women change.

212
01:20:19.906 --> 01:20:23.906
Into godly men and godly women in the name of Jesus.

213
01:20:23.906 --> 01:20:25.906
But that is work.

214
01:20:25.906 --> 01:20:28.906
You must understand, there is work to be done.

215
01:20:28.906 --> 01:20:30.906
Helping people.

216
01:20:30.906 --> 01:20:36.906
So that they will ultimately change into their original creation.

217
01:20:36.906 --> 01:20:37.906
That is work.

218
01:20:37.906 --> 01:20:41.906
For we all have that spirit, soul, and body.

219
01:20:42.906 --> 01:20:47.906
And to get that body and soul aligned with the right spiritual mindset,

220
01:20:47.906 --> 01:20:48.906
that is work.

221
01:20:48.906 --> 01:20:53.906
For Paul says, the flesh and the spirit are always in conflict with each other.

222
01:20:53.906 --> 01:20:59.906
So it is not the case that we may lead the church in the way of,

223
01:20:59.906 --> 01:21:05.906
as long as we create a nice experience, then we have done well.

224
01:21:06.906 --> 01:21:11.906
And whether you want your flesh to be submissive to the right spiritual mindset,

225
01:21:11.906 --> 01:21:12.906
I don't care.

226
01:21:12.906 --> 01:21:16.906
If I do that, then we might have a good time for one generation.

227
01:21:16.906 --> 01:21:19.906
But then everything falls apart.

228
01:21:19.906 --> 01:21:23.906
Then it goes wrong.

229
01:21:23.906 --> 01:21:25.906
Then it goes off the rails.

230
01:21:25.906 --> 01:21:30.906
Then it collapses, then it implodes, explodes, however you want to call it.

231
01:21:30.906 --> 01:21:33.906
God does not give His approval to that either.

232
01:21:33.906 --> 01:21:37.906
And if God does not take such approval, then it says in the book of Revelation,

233
01:21:37.906 --> 01:21:41.906
then Jesus says, I will take away the lampstand.

234
01:21:41.906 --> 01:21:43.906
And that is serious.

235
01:21:43.906 --> 01:21:47.906
Jesus says to the Ephesian church, if you do not stop that behavior,

236
01:21:47.906 --> 01:21:50.906
then I must remove the lampstand.

237
01:21:50.906 --> 01:21:52.906
And that is spiritual language.

238
01:21:52.906 --> 01:21:55.906
The lampstand was the flame in the church.

239
01:21:55.906 --> 01:21:58.906
And the flame represents the ministry in the church.

240
01:21:58.906 --> 01:22:00.906
And that ministry must continue.

241
01:22:00.906 --> 01:22:02.906
It must always continue.

242
01:22:02.906 --> 01:22:06.906
Consistently, that flame must remain lit.

243
01:22:06.906 --> 01:22:11.906
And when Jesus says, I want you to serve the church in a pure and holy way.

244
01:22:11.906 --> 01:22:12.906
Not just now.

245
01:22:12.906 --> 01:22:14.906
Not just now to have fun in the present.

246
01:22:14.906 --> 01:22:16.906
No, but for generations to come.

247
01:22:16.906 --> 01:22:20.906
A house of the generations.

248
01:22:20.906 --> 01:22:26.906
And I want, dear Jesus, I want the lampstand to keep burning.

249
01:22:26.906 --> 01:22:30.906
Until the return of our Lord and Master King Jesus.

250
01:22:30.906 --> 01:22:35.906
And that is why we must handle this church with care.

251
01:22:35.906 --> 01:22:37.906
For it is a precious church.

252
01:22:37.906 --> 01:22:39.906
It is not bragging.

253
01:22:39.906 --> 01:22:41.906
But this is a wonderful church.

254
01:22:41.906 --> 01:22:42.906
I feel good here.

255
01:22:42.906 --> 01:22:43.906
I want to be here.

256
01:22:43.906 --> 01:22:44.906
Here is where I want to be.

257
01:22:44.906 --> 01:22:46.906
In this church.

258
01:22:46.906 --> 01:22:48.906
When I go on vacation, I sometimes visit other churches.

259
01:22:48.906 --> 01:22:50.906
Then I think, that's really nice.

260
01:22:50.906 --> 01:22:51.906
Brothers and sisters.

261
01:22:51.906 --> 01:22:54.906
You always have a nice resonance with the brothers and sisters.

262
01:22:54.906 --> 01:22:58.906
Whether you are in Italy, whether you are in France, whether you are in Spain.

263
01:22:58.906 --> 01:23:00.906
It is always nice when you meet Christians.

264
01:23:00.906 --> 01:23:02.906
Yes, that is the same behavior.

265
01:23:02.906 --> 01:23:03.906
That is nice.

266
01:23:03.906 --> 01:23:05.906
But then I come home to my own congregation.

267
01:23:05.906 --> 01:23:07.906
And then I think, ah, I love these people.

268
01:23:07.906 --> 01:23:08.906
The churches are so nice.

269
01:23:08.906 --> 01:23:11.906
I love these people.

270
01:23:11.906 --> 01:23:15.906
And that's why I said to the leaders, pay attention, the church is growing.

271
01:23:15.906 --> 01:23:17.906
Pay attention.

272
01:23:17.906 --> 01:23:21.906
Because a growing church also brings its challenges.

273
01:23:21.906 --> 01:23:24.906
It brings its challenges with it.

274
01:23:24.906 --> 01:23:26.906
And that's what I wanted to talk about.

275
01:23:26.906 --> 01:23:32.906
If you have brought the Bible with you, then go with me to the book of Acts.

276
01:23:32.906 --> 01:23:33.906
Of course.

277
01:23:33.906 --> 01:23:38.906
Because when you talk about church building, you go to Acts.

278
01:23:38.906 --> 01:23:44.906
I said to the leaders, how cool is it, how amazing, wonderfully cool it is,

279
01:23:44.906 --> 01:23:47.906
that we have the book of Acts.

280
01:23:47.906 --> 01:23:49.906
Jesus has been.

281
01:23:49.906 --> 01:23:51.906
We have the four gospels.

282
01:23:51.906 --> 01:23:54.906
Jesus dies on the cross, rises from a grave.

283
01:23:54.906 --> 01:23:56.906
Vanessa emphasized this again.

284
01:23:56.906 --> 01:24:00.906
We must continue to echo the gospel in this church every time.

285
01:24:00.906 --> 01:24:02.906
That the gospel is clear.

286
01:24:02.906 --> 01:24:05.906
We are not here for all kinds of concepts.

287
01:24:05.906 --> 01:24:08.906
We are here for the clear gospel.

288
01:24:08.906 --> 01:24:14.906
Jesus came to restore humanity to the Father.

289
01:24:14.906 --> 01:24:16.906
He did this by dying on a cross.

290
01:24:16.906 --> 01:24:20.906
By rising, physically dying on a cross.

291
01:24:20.906 --> 01:24:23.906
A real human of flesh and blood.

292
01:24:23.906 --> 01:24:27.906
Just like you, just like me, died on a cross.

293
01:24:27.906 --> 01:24:32.906
Then he literally, physically goes into a grave.

294
01:24:32.906 --> 01:24:34.906
Stone in front of it.

295
01:24:34.906 --> 01:24:37.906
After three days, so not after a few hours.

296
01:24:37.906 --> 01:24:40.906
So you could say, maybe he was just unconscious.

297
01:24:40.906 --> 01:24:44.906
No, literally three days he was in a grave.

298
01:24:44.906 --> 01:24:47.906
After three days he rises from a grave.

299
01:24:47.906 --> 01:24:50.906
Physically, not as a mirage.

300
01:24:51.906 --> 01:24:54.906
Not as a myth, not as a mystery.

301
01:24:54.906 --> 01:24:58.906
Not as, how nice he was, he lives on in us.

302
01:24:58.906 --> 01:24:59.906
That is not it.

303
01:24:59.906 --> 01:25:02.906
A physical man rose from a grave.

304
01:25:02.906 --> 01:25:06.906
And he showed himself to more than five hundred witnesses.

305
01:25:06.906 --> 01:25:09.906
And then he physically ascends to heaven.

306
01:25:09.906 --> 01:25:13.906
He literally ascended to heaven.

307
01:25:13.906 --> 01:25:15.906
Until they no longer saw him.

308
01:25:15.906 --> 01:25:19.906
And two men in white said, why are you standing looking up into heaven?

309
01:25:19.906 --> 01:25:25.906
Just as this Jesus went physically to heaven.

310
01:25:25.906 --> 01:25:28.906
So he will also return.

311
01:25:28.906 --> 01:25:31.906
So there is no discussion possible if you say to me.

312
01:25:31.906 --> 01:25:36.906
Yes, the second coming may be a concept.

313
01:25:36.906 --> 01:25:39.906
Yes, the second coming may have already happened.

314
01:25:39.906 --> 01:25:41.906
He lives on in us.

315
01:25:41.906 --> 01:25:43.906
Yes, the second coming.

316
01:25:43.906 --> 01:25:44.906
Yes, the second coming.

317
01:25:44.906 --> 01:25:45.906
No, nothing.

318
01:25:45.906 --> 01:25:46.906
Yes, the second coming.

319
01:25:46.906 --> 01:25:49.906
He will return just as he came.

320
01:25:49.906 --> 01:25:58.906
And when he returns, then the reign of King Jesus begins for which he died.

321
01:25:58.906 --> 01:26:02.906
He died to be able to reign.

322
01:26:02.906 --> 01:26:04.906
Even if he had not died for us.

323
01:26:04.906 --> 01:26:06.906
Even if he had sinned in the desert.

324
01:26:06.906 --> 01:26:10.906
Even if he had thought to himself, you can deal with it.

325
01:26:10.906 --> 01:26:12.906
You bunch of fools, I'm out of here.

326
01:26:12.906 --> 01:26:18.906
Even if he had thought that, he would not have had the right to reign.

327
01:26:18.906 --> 01:26:20.906
For he was on a mission.

328
01:26:20.906 --> 01:26:28.906
In obedience to the Father, he was on a mission to fulfill what the Father commanded him.

329
01:26:28.906 --> 01:26:35.906
And therefore he will return as Lord and Master over all of creation.

330
01:26:35.906 --> 01:26:40.906
And those who are in Christ may reign together with him.

331
01:26:40.906 --> 01:26:43.906
So important to hold on to the gospel.

332
01:26:43.906 --> 01:26:45.906
In Jesus' name.

333
01:26:45.906 --> 01:26:53.906
And so when we talk about a mission and a goal, what you must do for God is very important.

334
01:26:53.906 --> 01:26:58.906
And you must hold on to that, I said to the leaders.

335
01:26:58.906 --> 01:27:01.906
You must hold on to your assignment.

336
01:27:01.906 --> 01:27:06.906
And you must guard that assignment in a growing church.

337
01:27:07.906 --> 01:27:15.906
That assignment, you must not let it be derailed in a growing church.

338
01:27:15.906 --> 01:27:19.906
In a growing church, many people come in.

339
01:27:19.906 --> 01:27:21.906
And all those people have opinions.

340
01:27:21.906 --> 01:27:24.906
And everything is going great and it's all fun.

341
01:27:24.906 --> 01:27:27.906
And everyone thinks it is a volunteer organization.

342
01:27:27.906 --> 01:27:31.906
And in a volunteer organization, we can all contribute something.

343
01:27:31.906 --> 01:27:33.906
And it's all cool and it's all good.

344
01:27:33.906 --> 01:27:40.906
But it is of vital importance for the leaders of the church that we hold on to our mission.

345
01:27:40.906 --> 01:27:43.906
And that we become unshakeable in that.

346
01:27:43.906 --> 01:27:44.906
In Jesus' name.

347
01:27:44.906 --> 01:27:47.906
Acts chapter 20 please.

348
01:27:47.906 --> 01:27:54.906
In Acts chapter 20 we read that Paul is on a mission.

349
01:27:54.906 --> 01:27:58.906
I believe the third mission towards Jerusalem.

350
01:27:58.906 --> 01:28:01.906
And Paul is on a mission.

351
01:28:01.906 --> 01:28:09.906
And that mission must be carried out as the Holy Spirit has given it to Paul.

352
01:28:09.906 --> 01:28:16.906
The Holy Spirit tells Paul this is your mission and you must go do it.

353
01:28:16.906 --> 01:28:20.906
And what you are going to do is suffer in the name of Jesus.

354
01:28:20.906 --> 01:28:24.906
And I don't mean suffering with a short 'ij', but it is suffering with a long 'ij'.

355
01:28:24.906 --> 01:28:31.906
Paul knew in advance that what I am going to do will have an effect for the whole world.

356
01:28:31.906 --> 01:28:37.906
Many people will come to believe in Jesus, but it will be accompanied by suffering with a long 'ij'.

357
01:28:37.906 --> 01:28:47.906
For being on a mission in God's kingdom is not just that God says I send you on a mission and you will become rich and everything will always go well with you.

358
01:28:47.906 --> 01:28:50.906
The mission of Jesus cost Jesus his life.

359
01:28:50.906 --> 01:28:53.906
The mission of Jesus cost him beatings.

360
01:28:53.906 --> 01:29:00.906
The mission of Paul cost him beatings and lashings and concrete blocks around his ankles.

361
01:29:00.906 --> 01:29:05.906
The missions of all twelve apostles cost them their lives.

362
01:29:05.906 --> 01:29:12.906
The mission we are on is not just fun and feeling good.

363
01:29:12.906 --> 01:29:16.906
It is a calling that we must guard with all that is within us.

364
01:29:16.906 --> 01:29:19.906
Acts chapter 20 verse 17.

365
01:29:19.906 --> 01:29:26.906
And so Paul is on his way to Jerusalem, but they are passing by Ephesus by boat.

366
01:29:26.906 --> 01:29:29.906
And Ephesus is the beloved church.

367
01:29:29.906 --> 01:29:34.906
Philippians, Philippi, and Ephesus are important churches for Paul.

368
01:29:34.906 --> 01:29:40.906
But instead of going there, he says I don't have time for that.

369
01:29:40.906 --> 01:29:44.906
I love Ephesus so much. I love them.

370
01:29:44.906 --> 01:29:47.906
And I would love to be with them.

371
01:29:47.906 --> 01:29:51.906
Enjoying intimacy and teaching for a few more months.

372
01:29:51.906 --> 01:29:54.906
Eating together and having a good time.

373
01:29:54.906 --> 01:29:57.906
The people in Ephesus were crazy about Paul.

374
01:29:57.906 --> 01:29:59.906
Paul had done miracles there.

375
01:29:59.906 --> 01:30:01.906
He explained the gospel there.

376
01:30:01.906 --> 01:30:04.906
He had had intimacy with them for several years.

377
01:30:04.906 --> 01:30:07.906
And now he is sailing past them.

378
01:30:07.906 --> 01:30:08.906
And there lies Ephesus.

379
01:30:08.906 --> 01:30:12.906
And before you know it, you would say to yourself.

380
01:30:12.906 --> 01:30:15.906
Yes, I am on a mission, but just a little detour.

381
01:30:15.906 --> 01:30:16.906
Just to Ephesus.

382
01:30:16.906 --> 01:30:18.906
Just to make it nice and cozy.

383
01:30:18.906 --> 01:30:22.906
But no, then he might have been there for months or maybe even years.

384
01:30:22.906 --> 01:30:25.906
Because Ephesus was so important to Paul.

385
01:30:25.906 --> 01:30:26.906
But he doesn't do that.

386
01:30:26.906 --> 01:30:28.906
Paul knows I am on a mission.

387
01:30:28.906 --> 01:30:31.906
Here is a lesson for us.

388
01:30:31.906 --> 01:30:35.906
When you are walking with God, you should not take detours.

389
01:30:35.906 --> 01:30:39.906
And being momentarily absent from your goal to move towards Jesus.

390
01:30:39.906 --> 01:30:42.906
No detours, we don't have time for that.

391
01:30:42.906 --> 01:30:44.906
Sometimes I see people coming back to the church.

392
01:30:44.906 --> 01:30:46.906
They have taken a whole detour.

393
01:30:46.906 --> 01:30:49.906
And then I think to myself, it's really nice that you are back.

394
01:30:49.906 --> 01:30:51.906
But you have wasted a few years.

395
01:30:51.906 --> 01:30:53.906
You have been away on a detour.

396
01:30:53.906 --> 01:30:56.906
Yes Tim, it has been difficult. I haven't been there for a while.

397
01:30:56.906 --> 01:30:59.906
Nice, there is grace to come back, just like the prodigal son.

398
01:30:59.906 --> 01:31:01.906
But why did you waste time?

399
01:31:01.906 --> 01:31:04.906
Be with the Lord. Go straight towards your goal.

400
01:31:04.906 --> 01:31:06.906
Stay with Jesus. Stay on His path.

401
01:31:06.906 --> 01:31:09.906
Keep loving Jesus. Keep reading His Word.

402
01:31:09.906 --> 01:31:11.906
No detours.

403
01:31:11.906 --> 01:31:13.906
Yes, but now I am tired, so I am going to step away for a moment.

404
01:31:13.906 --> 01:31:15.906
Well, I am disappointed, so I am going to step away for a moment.

405
01:31:15.906 --> 01:31:18.906
No, no detours. Not to the right, not to the left.

406
01:31:18.906 --> 01:31:20.906
Straight towards your goal, in Jesus' name.

407
01:31:20.906 --> 01:31:21.906
Hallelujah.

408
01:31:21.906 --> 01:31:24.906
And Paul does this here, even though he loves Ephesus.

409
01:31:24.906 --> 01:31:27.906
He says, I am on a mission to Jerusalem.

410
01:31:27.906 --> 01:31:30.906
I love these guys, but I am heading towards my goal.

411
01:31:30.906 --> 01:31:32.906
No time to waste.

412
01:31:33.906 --> 01:31:34.906
Verse 17.

413
01:31:34.906 --> 01:31:39.906
But from Miletus he sent someone to Ephesus.

414
01:31:39.906 --> 01:31:42.906
So instead of going to Ephesus himself,

415
01:31:42.906 --> 01:31:46.906
he sends someone to Ephesus and says, you know what we will do?

416
01:31:46.906 --> 01:31:48.906
Then we will have a leaders' meeting for a moment.

417
01:31:48.906 --> 01:31:49.906
That is what is going to happen here.

418
01:31:49.906 --> 01:31:55.906
This man had to ask the leaders of the congregation there to come to Paul.

419
01:31:55.906 --> 01:32:00.906
When they had come to him, he took leave of them.

420
01:32:00.906 --> 01:32:05.906
For Paul knew by the Holy Spirit, this is it.

421
01:32:05.906 --> 01:32:08.906
I'm going to my end.

422
01:32:08.906 --> 01:32:14.906
So Paul says, this is not a pleasant time, this is farewell time.

423
01:32:14.906 --> 01:32:19.906
He said, you know how I used to behave among you.

424
01:32:19.906 --> 01:32:27.906
From the day I set foot in Asia among you, I have served the Lord humbly.

425
01:32:27.906 --> 01:32:32.906
If you take notes in your own Bible, then I want to say to the whole church,

426
01:32:32.906 --> 01:32:36.906
when you serve the Lord, serve Him humbly.

427
01:32:36.906 --> 01:32:40.906
Do not serve Him like a show-off, but serve Him humbly.

428
01:32:40.906 --> 01:32:44.906
Know who the Lord is in relation to who you are.

429
01:32:44.906 --> 01:32:47.906
I have prayed for you with tears.

430
01:32:47.906 --> 01:32:52.906
I saw a leader crying during a prayer last weekend.

431
01:32:52.906 --> 01:32:55.906
Prayed with tears for the church.

432
01:32:55.906 --> 01:33:00.906
Why pray with tears? Because then you feel the heart of God.

433
01:33:00.906 --> 01:33:09.906
The heart of God is that He wants you to have a pure, holy, wonderful, and peaceful life in Christ.

434
01:33:09.906 --> 01:33:12.906
And sometimes that is a struggle and a fight.

435
01:33:12.906 --> 01:33:15.906
And you must feel that fight within you.

436
01:33:15.906 --> 01:33:17.906
And sometimes that brings tears.

437
01:33:17.906 --> 01:33:19.906
And sometimes that brings toil.

438
01:33:19.906 --> 01:33:21.906
And sometimes that brings conflicting times.

439
01:33:21.906 --> 01:33:25.906
And that is why Paul says, I have prayed for you with tears.

440
01:33:25.906 --> 01:33:30.906
Even though I have had many difficulties because the Jews tried to kill me.

441
01:33:30.906 --> 01:33:32.906
Verse 20 you may underline.

442
01:33:32.906 --> 01:33:39.906
I have done everything to teach you all that is good for you.

443
01:33:39.906 --> 01:33:48.906
Open church does everything to teach you all that is good for you.

444
01:33:48.906 --> 01:33:51.906
Open church, I'm talking to you.

445
01:33:51.906 --> 01:33:58.906
We truly do everything to teach you all that is good for you.

446
01:33:58.906 --> 01:34:01.906
God's Word is good for you.

447
01:34:01.906 --> 01:34:06.906
And sometimes we will present God's Word to you that you think to yourself,

448
01:34:06.906 --> 01:34:10.906
ah, then it cuts into your flesh.

449
01:34:10.906 --> 01:34:17.906
But we do everything to teach you all that is good for you.

450
01:34:17.906 --> 01:34:19.906
The Bible is good for you.

451
01:34:19.906 --> 01:34:23.906
Even when there is a correction, it is good for you.

452
01:34:23.906 --> 01:34:28.906
We have no profit-seeking in our minds.

453
01:34:28.906 --> 01:34:30.906
We do not want to become richer from you.

454
01:34:30.906 --> 01:34:32.906
We want you to become better.

455
01:34:32.906 --> 01:34:35.906
We want you to benefit from it.

456
01:34:35.906 --> 01:34:38.906
We want you to stand before the King pure and holy.

457
01:34:38.906 --> 01:34:40.906
This is what we want.

458
01:34:40.906 --> 01:34:41.906
This is our goal.

459
01:34:41.906 --> 01:34:44.906
We talk and pray about this during the Leaders' Weekend.

460
01:34:44.906 --> 01:34:46.906
We do everything for that.

461
01:34:46.906 --> 01:34:50.906
On the street, in the synagogue, and at people's homes.

462
01:34:50.906 --> 01:34:55.906
I have already told Jews and Greeks that they must henceforth focus on God

463
01:34:55.906 --> 01:34:59.906
and believe in our Lord, Jesus.

464
01:34:59.906 --> 01:35:02.906
Now I am traveling to Jerusalem.

465
01:35:02.906 --> 01:35:04.906
You should take a good look at these words.

466
01:35:04.906 --> 01:35:07.906
As a prisoner of the Holy Spirit.

467
01:35:07.906 --> 01:35:11.906
Check those words, study along with me.

468
01:35:11.906 --> 01:35:16.906
Now I am traveling to Jerusalem as a prisoner of the Holy Spirit.

469
01:35:16.906 --> 01:35:18.906
What does this mean?

470
01:35:18.906 --> 01:35:23.906
That Paul knew what his mission was.

471
01:35:23.906 --> 01:35:25.906
And he could not deviate from that.

472
01:35:25.906 --> 01:35:27.906
That is what that means.

473
01:35:27.906 --> 01:35:29.906
The Holy Spirit says you are going to Jerusalem.

474
01:35:29.906 --> 01:35:32.906
For in Jerusalem you must suffer much for me.

475
01:35:32.906 --> 01:35:38.906
And through your suffering, I can explosively expand the gospel to the whole world.

476
01:35:38.906 --> 01:35:43.906
This is a climax moment in Paul's ministry.

477
01:35:43.906 --> 01:35:50.906
And so being a prisoner of the Holy Spirit means that you know what you must do.

478
01:35:50.906 --> 01:35:54.906
And that is a time, dear people, in your life.

479
01:35:54.906 --> 01:35:58.906
It is a process where you ultimately know who you are and what you must do.

480
01:35:58.906 --> 01:36:07.906
I know by now, I said, I know by now what I must do.

481
01:36:07.906 --> 01:36:14.906
I have been leading this church for ten years now, but I have come to know what I really need to do.

482
01:36:14.906 --> 01:36:18.906
So not what the expectation is of what I should do.

483
01:36:18.906 --> 01:36:22.906
Not what people think I should do.

484
01:36:22.906 --> 01:36:25.906
Not what I think I should do.

485
01:36:25.906 --> 01:36:29.906
For what do I think of myself? Yes, I picked that up from other stories.

486
01:36:29.906 --> 01:36:34.906
I should not do what I must do based on the behavior of other people.

487
01:36:34.906 --> 01:36:40.906
But I must do what I need to do because the Holy Spirit tells me to.

488
01:36:40.906 --> 01:36:43.906
And that is a process of growth.

489
01:36:43.906 --> 01:36:49.906
It is arrogance to think that as soon as you come to repentance, you immediately know who you are.

490
01:36:49.906 --> 01:36:53.906
And I will immediately say it and I will immediately start to turn and I will immediately...

491
01:36:53.906 --> 01:36:55.906
That is completely not true.

492
01:36:55.906 --> 01:36:59.906
First discipleship, then being an apostle.

493
01:36:59.906 --> 01:37:02.906
First learn, learn, learn, learn, learn.

494
01:37:02.906 --> 01:37:05.906
And once you have learned, you need to learn even more.

495
01:37:05.906 --> 01:37:08.906
And once you have learned even more, you need to go learn again...

496
01:37:08.906 --> 01:37:11.906
...because you found out that you have taken a few detours.

497
01:37:11.906 --> 01:37:13.906
It is a process.

498
01:37:13.906 --> 01:37:16.906
I now know what I need to do.

499
01:37:16.906 --> 01:37:23.906
My task is to be a shepherd over the open church and to be a teacher in the open church.

500
01:37:23.906 --> 01:37:29.906
It is not my task to go out into the world at this moment, now in my life.

501
01:37:29.906 --> 01:37:32.906
It is not my task to go to other churches.

502
01:37:32.906 --> 01:37:35.906
I have very little to do with churches in Amsterdam and Rotterdam.

503
01:37:35.906 --> 01:37:37.906
Really nice for those Christians there.

504
01:37:37.906 --> 01:37:40.906
I have house remnants in open church.

505
01:37:40.906 --> 01:37:42.906
You will see me here.

506
01:37:42.906 --> 01:37:45.906
I am not allowed to speak out except with Ivan and Sadis.

507
01:37:45.906 --> 01:37:51.906
I know that I have grounds there to share the gospel with Vanessa, together with Ivan and Sadis...

508
01:37:51.906 --> 01:37:55.906
...missionaries from Cuba in Spain to be able to give.

509
01:37:55.906 --> 01:37:57.906
But otherwise you won't see me anywhere.

510
01:37:57.906 --> 01:38:00.906
I have no feeling for it. It doesn't resonate within me.

511
01:38:00.906 --> 01:38:04.906
Why? Because I feel that I am captured by the Holy Spirit.

512
01:38:04.906 --> 01:38:10.906
That is why I say house rest. I feel captured by the Holy Spirit to do this.

513
01:38:10.906 --> 01:38:15.906
And I will continue to do this until I am sure that it is full.

514
01:38:15.906 --> 01:38:17.906
For that is also what Paul will say shortly.

515
01:38:17.906 --> 01:38:19.906
So when we read in verse 22...

516
01:38:19.906 --> 01:38:24.906
...now I am on my way to Jerusalem as a prisoner of the Holy Spirit.

517
01:38:24.906 --> 01:38:27.906
Do not be alarmed, but what Paul means by that...

518
01:38:27.906 --> 01:38:31.906
...I have a mission from the Holy Spirit and I must not deviate from it.

519
01:38:31.906 --> 01:38:37.906
Focus. Pay attention, the church is growing. Pay attention, you have a task.

520
01:38:37.906 --> 01:38:41.906
I do not know exactly what will happen to me there.

521
01:38:41.906 --> 01:38:43.906
Pay attention to what is written here in verse 23.

522
01:38:43.906 --> 01:38:47.906
I only know that chains and difficulties await me in Jerusalem...

523
01:38:47.906 --> 01:38:49.906
...for the Holy Spirit tells me that in every city.

524
01:38:49.906 --> 01:38:51.906
Is that intense or intense?

525
01:38:55.906 --> 01:38:59.906
But I find all of that not important at all.

526
01:38:59.906 --> 01:39:03.906
I find nothing important, not even my own life.

527
01:39:03.906 --> 01:39:08.906
I want to gladly do everything that Jesus asks of me.

528
01:39:08.906 --> 01:39:15.906
The task He has given me, I want to complete it fully.

529
01:39:15.906 --> 01:39:20.906
I also want to complete my task fully.

530
01:39:20.906 --> 01:39:27.906
Do you also want to complete your task with the Lord fully?

531
01:39:27.906 --> 01:39:30.906
Let's take a moment to pause for ten seconds on that.

532
01:39:30.906 --> 01:39:35.906
That you say in your soul, Lord, truly, I want to complete my task.

533
01:39:35.906 --> 01:39:39.906
I want to fulfill what I must do. Truly.

534
01:39:39.906 --> 01:39:42.906
And what Paul says in the verse before that is...

535
01:39:42.906 --> 01:39:45.906
...nothing is more important than completing that task.

536
01:39:45.906 --> 01:39:48.906
I want to complete that task, I need to pay attention to that.

537
01:39:48.906 --> 01:39:50.906
I want to complete that task.

538
01:39:50.906 --> 01:39:54.906
Maybe you think to yourself, I still don't know what my task is.

539
01:39:54.906 --> 01:39:56.906
And that's fine.

540
01:39:56.906 --> 01:40:02.906
Because if you still don't know what your task is, then you are still in discipleship mode.

541
01:40:02.906 --> 01:40:06.906
And the mode of discipleship has just one task, to learn.

542
01:40:06.906 --> 01:40:08.906
Learn, learn, learn.

543
01:40:08.906 --> 01:40:10.906
Grow, grow, grow.

544
01:40:10.906 --> 01:40:12.906
Be formed, be formed.

545
01:40:12.906 --> 01:40:14.906
That is your task.

546
01:40:14.906 --> 01:40:19.906
So, if you still do not know what your intrinsic task is...

547
01:40:19.906 --> 01:40:21.906
...captured by the Holy Spirit...

548
01:40:21.906 --> 01:40:23.906
...do not worry.

549
01:40:23.906 --> 01:40:26.906
Be a faithful disciple of Jesus.

550
01:40:26.906 --> 01:40:28.906
That is your task.

551
01:40:28.906 --> 01:40:31.906
For if you are a faithful disciple of Jesus...

552
01:40:31.906 --> 01:40:33.906
...and He may guide you...

553
01:40:33.906 --> 01:40:36.906
...even without detours...

554
01:40:36.906 --> 01:40:39.906
...also during your discipleship do not say...

555
01:40:39.906 --> 01:40:42.906
...yes, well, I will just go look there, well I will just go look there...

556
01:40:42.906 --> 01:40:44.906
...no, faithful discipleship.

557
01:40:44.906 --> 01:40:46.906
Continue, holy, pure.

558
01:40:46.906 --> 01:40:48.906
Continue with Jesus.

559
01:40:48.906 --> 01:40:50.906
Then ultimately He can say...

560
01:40:50.906 --> 01:40:52.906
...ah, that is a faithful disciple.

561
01:40:52.906 --> 01:40:54.906
I can use Him.

562
01:40:54.906 --> 01:40:57.906
He has taught me to understand His voice over the years.

563
01:40:57.906 --> 01:41:00.906
Jesus says, my sheep recognize my voice.

564
01:41:00.906 --> 01:41:02.906
You need to train yourself in that...

565
01:41:02.906 --> 01:41:05.906
...to learn to understand the voice of the Holy Spirit.

566
01:41:05.906 --> 01:41:07.906
And then ultimately He says...

567
01:41:07.906 --> 01:41:09.906
...at a mature moment He says...

568
01:41:09.906 --> 01:41:11.906
...I have a mission for you.

569
01:41:11.906 --> 01:41:13.906
You must go into the mission field.

570
01:41:13.906 --> 01:41:15.906
I have a mission for you.

571
01:41:15.906 --> 01:41:17.906
You will establish a church.

572
01:41:17.906 --> 01:41:19.906
I have a mission for you. You will teach.

573
01:41:19.906 --> 01:41:21.906
And then you understand that mission.

574
01:41:21.906 --> 01:41:23.906
And then you can say it...

575
01:41:23.906 --> 01:41:25.906
...and I want to finish it.

576
01:41:25.906 --> 01:41:27.906
In Jesus' name.

577
01:41:27.906 --> 01:41:30.906
Paul says in verse 24b...

578
01:41:30.906 --> 01:41:33.906
...that task is to tell the good news of God's...

579
01:41:33.906 --> 01:41:36.906
...loving goodness to the people.

580
01:41:36.906 --> 01:41:40.906
I have also spoken to you about the kingdom of God.

581
01:41:40.906 --> 01:41:43.906
I know that you will not see me again.

582
01:41:43.906 --> 01:41:44.906
Wow.

583
01:41:44.906 --> 01:41:47.906
That is why I say clearly today...

584
01:41:47.906 --> 01:41:49.906
...that it is not my fault...

585
01:41:49.906 --> 01:41:53.906
...if someone dies without believing in Jesus.

586
01:41:53.906 --> 01:41:55.906
Is that a heavy verse or not?

587
01:41:55.906 --> 01:41:57.906
In other words, Paul is saying here...

588
01:41:57.906 --> 01:41:59.906
...I have done everything I could...

589
01:41:59.906 --> 01:42:01.906
...for the people in my area to know Jesus.

590
01:42:01.906 --> 01:42:04.906
That is a very confronting verse for me as well.

591
01:42:04.906 --> 01:42:07.906
That is a very confronting verse for you as well.

592
01:42:07.906 --> 01:42:11.906
Have you done everything you could for the people in your circle of life?

593
01:42:11.906 --> 01:42:15.906
That they at least know that they may give their lives to Jesus, must give?

594
01:42:15.906 --> 01:42:18.906
Have you done everything for that?

595
01:42:18.906 --> 01:42:22.906
Have at least your colleagues been informed...

596
01:42:22.906 --> 01:42:25.906
...that there is a living God in heaven...

597
01:42:25.906 --> 01:42:27.906
...to whom we must be reconciled?

598
01:42:27.906 --> 01:42:29.906
Have we done everything for that?

599
01:42:29.906 --> 01:42:31.906
I have neglected that for years.

600
01:42:31.906 --> 01:42:34.906
I have neglected that for years...

601
01:42:34.906 --> 01:42:38.906
...that I had little interest in telling other people...

602
01:42:38.906 --> 01:42:43.906
...about the necessity and urgency that we must be healed and saved from our sins.

603
01:42:43.906 --> 01:42:45.906
That is amazing.

604
01:42:45.906 --> 01:42:47.906
And so what Paul says here...

605
01:42:47.906 --> 01:42:52.906
...I know, says Paul, it is not my fault if someone dies without believing in Jesus...

606
01:42:52.906 --> 01:42:57.906
...for I have told everyone in my circle of life about the importance of Jesus Christ.

607
01:42:57.906 --> 01:42:59.906
It's intense that he says that.

608
01:42:59.906 --> 01:43:06.906
27. For without ceasing I have told you the whole Word of God.

609
01:43:06.906 --> 01:43:11.906
This is one of the objectives of Open Church...

610
01:43:11.906 --> 01:43:17.906
...to teach you the whole Word of God without ceasing.

611
01:43:17.906 --> 01:43:21.906
Open Church is not a place you can come to...

612
01:43:21.906 --> 01:43:25.906
...where you will hear topical sermons...

613
01:43:25.906 --> 01:43:28.906
...from one time this and another time that...

614
01:43:28.906 --> 01:43:32.906
...and a little topic here and now I find it fun to talk about that.

615
01:43:32.906 --> 01:43:34.906
We do not do this in Open Church.

616
01:43:34.906 --> 01:43:39.906
Open Church is a type of church where you come for God's Word.

617
01:43:39.906 --> 01:43:43.906
And now I will tell you about the Leadership weekend...

618
01:43:43.906 --> 01:43:46.906
...but very soon, probably next week...

619
01:43:46.906 --> 01:43:50.906
...we will start with the Ezra Bible study.

620
01:43:51.906 --> 01:43:53.906
I would actually start with Genesis...

621
01:43:53.906 --> 01:44:01.906
...because I want to do Genesis because of A House of the Generations.

622
01:44:01.906 --> 01:44:06.906
And I actually want to do Genesis to show the generations in Genesis.

623
01:44:06.906 --> 01:44:11.906
Only God has given me so many wow moments in the last few weeks...

624
01:44:11.906 --> 01:44:16.906
...from the Ezra story regarding the new construction.

625
01:44:17.906 --> 01:44:21.906
Yes, if that lives in me, then I just want to do Ezra.

626
01:44:21.906 --> 01:44:24.906
So we are going to do Ezra soon. Awesome.

627
01:44:24.906 --> 01:44:28.906
And so what is our task, verse 27?

628
01:44:28.906 --> 01:44:34.906
We will just continue on Sunday mornings to tell you the whole Word of God.

629
01:44:34.906 --> 01:44:38.906
Whether it is the prophets, or whether it is the Lamentations...

630
01:44:38.906 --> 01:44:41.906
...or whether it is the gospels, the letters.

631
01:44:41.906 --> 01:44:45.906
You will hear this whole Bible over the years in Open Church.

632
01:44:45.906 --> 01:44:49.906
For this whole Word is Jesus Christ our Lord.

633
01:44:49.906 --> 01:44:52.906
And now he comes, verse 28.

634
01:44:52.906 --> 01:45:01.906
Pay attention to yourselves and to the whole flock of which you are the leaders.

635
01:45:01.906 --> 01:45:07.906
Pay attention to yourself, two points, and to the flock.

636
01:45:08.906 --> 01:45:11.906
Pay attention to yourself, pay attention to the flock.

637
01:45:11.906 --> 01:45:14.906
Pay attention to yourself, pay attention to the flock.

638
01:45:14.906 --> 01:45:21.906
Pay attention to yourself in the sense of, are you as a leader still engaged with Jesus?

639
01:45:21.906 --> 01:45:24.906
Are you really engaged with Jesus?

640
01:45:24.906 --> 01:45:30.906
Or are you just fulfilling a task...

641
01:45:30.906 --> 01:45:37.906
...out of habit, out of a sense of obligation, out of tradition, out of identity?

642
01:45:37.906 --> 01:45:46.906
I said last weekend, no one can pin their task to their identity.

643
01:45:46.906 --> 01:45:52.906
Laura cannot say, I am a pianist.

644
01:45:52.906 --> 01:45:55.906
That is not your identity.

645
01:45:55.906 --> 01:45:59.906
Her identity is daughter of God.

646
01:46:01.906 --> 01:46:09.906
And you play piano from the captivity of the Holy Spirit and the task you then have to do.

647
01:46:09.906 --> 01:46:18.906
But if the Holy Spirit decides to send Roy and Laura next week to the Middle East...

648
01:46:18.906 --> 01:46:21.906
...I'm just saying, then that is the task.

649
01:46:21.906 --> 01:46:32.906
So it is very dangerous when people tie their position in the church to themselves as, this is my identity.

650
01:46:32.906 --> 01:46:39.906
Because another danger in that is, if that place were to pass, for example.

651
01:46:39.906 --> 01:46:41.906
If that place were to change.

652
01:46:41.906 --> 01:46:46.906
If God has a different idea than what you think your place is.

653
01:46:47.906 --> 01:46:51.906
Maybe God says, you just saw Caroline standing here singing.

654
01:46:51.906 --> 01:46:57.906
Maybe God says, I have someone else I want to place there now and I have a new season for her.

655
01:46:57.906 --> 01:47:05.906
But if she pins herself to her identity of the place and the task she has been given, you have a great conflict within yourself.

656
01:47:05.906 --> 01:47:07.906
Yes, but I am that.

657
01:47:07.906 --> 01:47:08.906
No, you are not that.

658
01:47:08.906 --> 01:47:11.906
You are a son or daughter of God.

659
01:47:11.906 --> 01:47:15.906
And you must position yourself as a servant for the Holy Spirit.

660
01:47:15.906 --> 01:47:20.906
So that you can always stay in tune for what you need to do for Him in Jesus' name. Amen.

661
01:47:20.906 --> 01:47:27.906
Take good care of yourself and of the whole flock of which you are leaders.

662
01:47:27.906 --> 01:47:34.906
If I have to pay attention to myself, then there are things I need to pay attention to about myself.

663
01:47:34.906 --> 01:47:40.906
One is that I come into contact with Jesus every day.

664
01:47:40.906 --> 01:47:43.906
That I am engaged with His Word every day.

665
01:47:43.906 --> 01:47:45.906
That I talk to Him every day.

666
01:47:45.906 --> 01:47:47.906
Take care of yourself, Tim.

667
01:47:47.906 --> 01:47:49.906
Don't overlook yourself.

668
01:47:49.906 --> 01:47:51.906
Don't be too busy with yourself.

669
01:47:51.906 --> 01:47:53.906
All busy, busy, busy.

670
01:47:53.906 --> 01:47:56.906
And then suddenly you have a day when you haven't talked to God.

671
01:47:56.906 --> 01:48:01.906
No, Tim. Take care of yourself, Paul says to the leaders in Ephesus.

672
01:48:01.906 --> 01:48:03.906
Take care of yourself.

673
01:48:03.906 --> 01:48:05.906
And Vanessa might say it once in a while.

674
01:48:05.906 --> 01:48:08.906
Hey, did you read your Bible today and what did you learn from your Bible today?

675
01:48:08.906 --> 01:48:10.906
And then we can have a nice conversation about that.

676
01:48:10.906 --> 01:48:14.906
But ultimately she cannot hold me responsible for what I need to do for myself.

677
01:48:14.906 --> 01:48:16.906
I need to be with Jesus.

678
01:48:16.906 --> 01:48:20.906
Take care of yourself, Tim. Take care of yourself.

679
01:48:20.906 --> 01:48:26.906
I need to keep a close watch on myself that I am with Jesus, reading His Word.

680
01:48:26.906 --> 01:48:29.906
That I do not fall for the temptations of this world.

681
01:48:29.906 --> 01:48:32.906
And that I will not be sidetracked by anyone.

682
01:48:32.906 --> 01:48:34.906
I must move towards my goal.

683
01:48:34.906 --> 01:48:38.906
I have been taken captive by the Holy Spirit for a purpose that I have.

684
01:48:38.906 --> 01:48:40.906
That way, together with Jesus.

685
01:48:40.906 --> 01:48:43.906
Whatever people think, whatever people say.

686
01:48:43.906 --> 01:48:46.906
The temptations of this world that come before me.

687
01:48:46.906 --> 01:48:49.906
Take care of yourself, Tim. I have a task and it is important.

688
01:48:49.906 --> 01:48:53.906
I cannot afford to be drunk.

689
01:48:53.906 --> 01:48:56.906
I cannot afford it, church.

690
01:48:56.906 --> 01:48:59.906
That someone from you meets me in Lommeldorp.

691
01:48:59.906 --> 01:49:02.906
Who says, Tim, he was off his path.

692
01:49:02.906 --> 01:49:04.906
I cannot afford that.

693
01:49:04.906 --> 01:49:06.906
I must take care of a church.

694
01:49:06.906 --> 01:49:08.906
I have two children at home.

695
01:49:08.906 --> 01:49:10.906
I have a wife for whom I must care.

696
01:49:10.906 --> 01:49:13.906
I cannot afford to be drunk or high.

697
01:49:13.906 --> 01:49:16.906
I cannot afford to speak useless language.

698
01:49:16.906 --> 01:49:19.906
I cannot afford to gossip about the people in the church.

699
01:49:19.906 --> 01:49:22.906
I cannot afford to walk away from this church.

700
01:49:22.906 --> 01:49:25.906
Suppose I would say from a moment of frustration, I quit.

701
01:49:25.906 --> 01:49:27.906
We all have a problem.

702
01:49:27.906 --> 01:49:29.906
That is not arrogance, but I have to do this.

703
01:49:29.906 --> 01:49:32.906
I am captured by the Holy Spirit to do what I must do.

704
01:49:32.906 --> 01:49:34.906
In Jesus' name.

705
01:49:34.906 --> 01:49:37.906
And so you must take care of yourself.

706
01:49:37.906 --> 01:49:40.906
And I said this to the leaders, but I also say this to you.

707
01:49:40.906 --> 01:49:43.906
The people of Open Church. Take care of yourself.

708
01:49:43.906 --> 01:49:45.906
You take care of yourself.

709
01:49:45.906 --> 01:49:47.906
You take care of yourself.

710
01:49:47.906 --> 01:49:50.906
And it is really great if you are here as a partner.

711
01:49:50.906 --> 01:49:53.906
If you are newly married, in a relationship.

712
01:49:53.906 --> 01:49:55.906
Parents with their children. That is all very nice.

713
01:49:55.906 --> 01:49:59.906
But ultimately you are a person with free will.

714
01:49:59.906 --> 01:50:01.906
You take care of you.

715
01:50:01.906 --> 01:50:03.906
In Jesus' name.

716
01:50:03.906 --> 01:50:08.906
And as we do that, we must also pay attention to the flock.

717
01:50:08.906 --> 01:50:11.906
Dear people, Open Church is a family.

718
01:50:11.906 --> 01:50:19.906
And the people in Open Church and the leaders in Open Church have the task of caring for this whole church.

719
01:50:19.906 --> 01:50:21.906
We must take care of you.

720
01:50:21.906 --> 01:50:23.906
That you are doing well.

721
01:50:23.906 --> 01:50:25.906
Not because we benefit from it.

722
01:50:25.906 --> 01:50:28.906
But we want marriages to be put on a better path.

723
01:50:28.906 --> 01:50:31.906
We want marriages to be blessed and holy.

724
01:50:31.906 --> 01:50:33.906
We want people to be baptized.

725
01:50:33.906 --> 01:50:36.906
Not out of hype, but out of awareness of sin.

726
01:50:36.906 --> 01:50:38.906
That people allow themselves to be baptized.

727
01:50:38.906 --> 01:50:40.906
That they know what it means to be baptized.

728
01:50:40.906 --> 01:50:43.906
And that they also know what it means to come out of the baptismal water.

729
01:50:43.906 --> 01:50:45.906
And not to immediately stay away the next day.

730
01:50:45.906 --> 01:50:47.906
We must take care of you.

731
01:50:47.906 --> 01:50:49.906
Just think about it.

732
01:50:50.906 --> 01:50:55.906
What do I care if you come out of the water and you're not here next week?

733
01:50:55.906 --> 01:50:57.906
I do care about that.

734
01:50:57.906 --> 01:50:59.906
Because we want things to go better for you.

735
